    "definitions": {
      "short": "a village (as covered in by walls); also a young lion (perhaps as covered with a mane)",
      "usage": "(young) lion, village. Compare 3723 .",
      "full": "H3715. kephir כְּפִיר noun masculine young lion ; — ׳כ Judg 14:5 16 t.; plural כְּפִרִים Jer 2:15 3 t.; כְּפִירִים Zech 11:3 7 t.; suffix כְּפִירַיִךְ Nahum 2:14; כְּפִירֶיהָ Ezek 38:13 (Co reads כנעניה ); — literal ׳כ אֲרָיוֺת Judg 14:5 young lion of lions ; Amos 3:4 ; Psa 17:12 . It differs from whelp גּוּר Ezek 19:2-3 ,as old enough to hunt its prey, Jer 25:38 ; Isa 11:6 ; Zech 11:3 ; Psa 104:21 ; in simile of roar of hostile army Isa 5:29 ׅ || (לָבִיא compare Jer 51:38 ׅ || אריות (גּוֺרֵי ; sim of ׳י s invincible might Isa 31:4 ׅ || (אַרְיֵה ; of Israel among the nations, Micah 5:7 ; of Assyr. princes Nahum 2:12 ; of prince of Israel Ezek 19:5-6 , other cases are: || לָבִיא Job 38:39 ; || שַׁחַל Hosea 5:14 ; Psa 91:13 ; Job 4:10 ; of bloodthirsty enemies Psa 34:11 ; 35:17 ; 58:7 ; Jer 2:15 ; ׳כ גוים Ezek 32:2 , of young warriors Nahum 2:14; 38:13 (?; see Co above); righteous compared with, Prov 28:1 ; king's wrath like roaring of, 19:12 ; 20:2 ; of one of faces of cherubim Ezek 41:19 .",
